      "side": 1,
      "message": "Julio: This is another old comment of mine that I wrote on a piece of paper. I wonder if we could come up with more informative names than `hash_value1` and `hash_value2`.\n\nI think we can probably describe `hash_value1` as the hash table bucket/slot index. Perhaps a shorter name would be  `lookup_table_index` because it is the index for the `p_hash_table-\u003ep_lookup_table[]` array.\n\nThen we need to find a more informative name for `hash_value2`. Perhaps `block_hash` or just `hash_value` if it is understood to be the hash value for a block?",
      "revId": "e91b7aa26d6d0979bba2bee5e1c27a7a695e0226",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
